<title>USA: Reliance Group Q4 net shr $0.30 vs $0.17.</title>
<headline>Reliance Group Q4 net shr $0.30 vs $0.17.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fourth Quarter Financial Highlights</p>
<p>		    (in millions, except per share amounts)</p>
<p>					  Quarter Ended</p>
<p>					   December 31</p>
<p>					    1996	1995 (1)</p>
<p> Total revenues			 $804.8    $734.4</p>
<p>Operating income excluding</p>
<p>  net realized capital gains	  29.5	18.0</p>
<p> Net income				 35.7	19.9</p>
<p>Per share information:</p>
<p>Operating income excluding</p>
<p>  net realized capital gains	   .25	 .15</p>
<p> Net income				  .30	 .17 (1)</p>
<p>NOTE: Operating and net income included an after-tax charge of $2.6 million ($.02 per share) in 1995 for Proposition 103.</p>
<p>		   Full Year Financial Highlights</p>
<p>		   (in millions, except per share amounts)</p>
<p>				  Year Ended		   Year Ended</p>
<p>			     Dec. 31, 1996		Dec. 31, 1995</p>
<p>	     Excluding asbestos and environmental charge(a)</p>
<p> Total revenues		 $3,090.6     $3,090.6    $2,906.0</p>
<p>Operating income</p>
<p>excluding net realized</p>
<p>  capital gains(1)		  16.0	  103.1	  76.4</p>
<p> Net income (1,2)		   48.2	  135.3	  88.1</p>
<p>Per share information:</p>
<p>Operating income</p>
<p>excluding net realized</p>
<p>  capital gains (1)		  .14	    .88	   .66</p>
<p> Net income (1,2,3)		  .41	   1.15	   .73</p>
<p>NOTE: (a) Excludes second quarter 1996 after-tax charge of $87.1 million, or $.74 per share, for increasing net loss reserves for asbestos-related and environmental pollution claims.</p>
<p>(1) Operating and net income included an after-tax charge of $2.6 million ($.02 per share) in 1995 for Proposition 103.</p>
<p>(2) Net income for the year ended December 31, 1995 included an after-tax charge of $4.5 million, or $.04 per share, on disposal of discontinued operations by an investee company and an after-tax charge of $3.4 million, or $.03 per share, for the early extinguishment of debt.</p>
<p>(3) Per share information for the year ended December 31, 1995 included a $.03 extraordinary charge relating to the early redemption of a subsidiary's preferred stock.</p>
